 - Writes require the `contributor` or `manager` role in the project. Users who can read but not write get 403.
 - Contributors may only modify tasks assigned to themselves, and may not reassign tasks. Managers may modify any task.
 - Only managers may delete tasks.
+- Moving a task (`/move`) removes it from its project, so it needs a manager
+  of the task's project. The destination must be readable by the user (else
+  404), a manager there (else 403), and not archived (else 409). Moving into
+  the task's own project → 400. The task keeps its ID, title, status and
+  assignee; if the assignee is not a contributor or manager of the destination,
+  the move is rejected with 400 and nothing changes.
 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
 
